Welcome to the void that is comp.sources.games.*. It was once a pleasant
place with free source code being posted occasionally and people happily 
working and hacking at games. Every new work in comp.source.games was a 
delight, crafted by someone with the urge to create something fun. It 
became a study of style and grace, a test of playability and portability,
a gem to be admired or one that needed "just a little more work." 

But the king has gone away and not come back. The castle is dusty, its 
halls filled with the sound of the echoing wind instead of the intense
and studied voices of those discussing the pros and cons of posted games.
The people of the village walk about as if in a dull trance. There is no 
reason to laugh or work on new and old games. The workshops are boarded
up and the tools rusting inside. Once, skilled craftsmen would come home 
from a long day at work and refine their games hoping one day to present
them to the king. He would study and critique it. And if all seemed well,
he would present it, wrapped in a shar file, to the public for all to see, 
use, and study. But now, there is no glory in working on such games. The 
king has gone away.

Occasionally, we hear the sounds of hooves clattering on the path into town 
and glance up in hope. But they are merely lost travelers who speak of 
games which have been bought and sold like harlots in the night. Toys 
made for profit, not for love of the craft. Each lost traveler diminishes 
our hopes for the safe return of our king. 

One day, we will hear pounding hooves as loud as thunder coming down the
path and we will look out from our behind our darkened hovels to see our
king (or his replacement) riding into town. And the rejoicing will begin.

Until then, all we have are stories and games of the past. 

